This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net.  Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.


1: You should be able to _ move to things like stairs and altars even
if their symbol is concealed by an item on the ground. -ekiM

2: When you try to apply something to an object at your feet (or to
loot a container on the ground) and there are multiple possible
targets, nethack should display a menu of targets rather than forcing
you to type 'n' repeatedly until you reach the desired object. -azgor

3: Neither gifts given to players from a deity nor quest artifacts
should appear in a bone file. -aristotle73

4: b!oGain Energy should grant sleep resistance for a couple of turns.
-Grunt

5:  Auto-stack option: When set to true, like items in inventory will
automatically stack upon identification. -aristotle73

6: The minetown watch needs to be more watchful - allowing violence in
the streets is unacceptable behaviour for any watch! -Grunt

7: A 'fork' tool, that when wielded allows you to eat deep-fried tins
without getting your hands greasy.  Also a handy weapon and engraving
tool. -Angcrist

8: "You dip your slime mold in the potion of acid. Your slime mold
dissolves! Your potion of acid turns into a potion of fruit juice!"
-GreyKnight

9: If you steal an item from a shop by teleporting or digging, it
should be possible to partially appease the shopkeeper by returning the
stolen item. But he/she won't do business with you until you also pay
them for their trouble. -azgor

10: When your hunger status is "weak", the player will get a message
"You eye the foo hungrily." when fighting a hostile foe.  A roll is
made based on luck and if successful the hostile foe will turn and
flee. -aristotle73

11: Pancakes thrown upwards should stick to the ceiling until someone
walks under it, where it drops down and blinds them. -LordMatthius

12: Teleportitis-granting corpses should teleport a pet if it's eaten
by them. -Grunt

13: (a)pplying a rubber hose to a fountain should make it into a fire
hose -- you will be prompted for a direction, and shoot a stream of
water in that direction (like a wand-zap).  Creatures hit by the stream
will be slowed and 'wet', with all the standard gush-of-water effects.
-workimer

14: (a)pplying a rubber hose to a fountain or pool could also prompt
you "Drink from the fire hose?  [y]" prior to letting you spray a
stream, with the expected amusing effects. -workimer

15: Dig spell/Wand of digging can be used to create a pit next to you
(to block off passageways and so on). -ekiM

16: For the DfVers: the Pick-axe of Anhur (named for the god most
followers of this style of play will follow); #invoke to use as a wand
of digging. -Grunt

17: a vampire next to a yellow light should get damaged by the light.
-paxed

18: A fire vortex or fire elemental stepping onto a space with a
spiderweb should burn away the web. -_NESoutlaw

19: sortloot + aforementioned autostack options. -mekkis

20: Archeologists should be immune to rolling boulder traps.
-LordMatthius

21: Cockatrice Golem - When wearing a ring of conflict it turns itself
to stone.  Otherwise, has more of a chance of stoning a player than a
normal cockatrice. -aristotle73

22: if you are levitating, zapping a /oFire should act as an
afterburner. ZOOOOOM. -braindancer

23: A #drag command should be entered, allowing players to drag corpses
along the ground, useful for taking them for sacrifice. -LordMatthius

24: A cursed unicorn horn should probably turn harmless potions into
harmful potions. -Grunt



Individual ideas may have contributions from multiple authors/editors,
